{
  "engine": "shadowkey",
  "about": "The Elder Scrolls Travels: Shadowkey, Vir2L's own engine. Sky, walls, floors and models (furniture, buildings, creatures) are captured as textured polygons after clipping, walls with their light as a palette chosen per pixel, models with the distance shade as vertex colours. The sky (the game's model fillers test depth against it) and the objects a player can target (the game picks targets from its own rasteriser's output) are captured but not skipped.",
  "viewport": {
    "width": 176,
    "height": 208
  },
